; CPUDETC.MAP -- the makecart recipe for the cpu_detect cartridge.
;
; A plain 8 KB cartridge is geometry and content, and nothing else:
;
;   CARTRIDGE   TYPE=1 is "standard 8 KB"; image size = BANKS * BANKSIZE.
;   IHEX        the Intel HEX from `orcalink --rom-config'.  Record
;               addresses are image offsets, not Atari addresses.  Every
;               byte no record covers is filled with $FF.
;
; No BANKVECTOR: the six bytes at $BFFA are the hardware's cartridge header,
; placed by the Intel HEX like every other byte.  No CARFS and no ADD, so no
; directory is built -- this cartridge holds no files.  No BANK/BANKORDER:
; one bank, no free area.
;
; Output: CPUDETC.MAP -> CPUDETC.CAR, next to the input (`makecart -o' overrides).

[MAP]
CARTRIDGE TYPE=1 BANKSIZE=8K BANKS=1
IHEX CPUDETC.HEX
